<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were lower in line with other European bonds in quiet late trade on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Bonos were subject to limited profit-taking after recent minor gains, they added. But in general trade was dull as players awaited new clues on the 1997 budget.</p>
<p>Members of the Catalan coalition CiU met the central goverment today to start discussing the budget, but no details were forthcoming.</p>
<p>Nevertheless, hopes of credible and austere measures should continue to underpin prices, dealers said.</p>
</text>
